{"node_id": "NRS_484B_270_2b_o3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-270-2b"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "When overtaking or passing", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "the driver of a motor vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "shall exercise due care and:", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "If there is only one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "pass to the left of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b8", "text": "at a safe distance, which must be not less than 3 feet between any portion of the vehicle and the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "and shall not move again to the right side of the highway", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b10", "text": "until the vehicle is safely clear of the overtaken bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "b11", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in NRS 484B.213 and 484B.217 [NRS-484B-213-1, NRS-484B-213-2a, NRS-484B-213-2b, NRS-484B-213-2c, NRS-484B-217-2],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "b12", "text": "when passing to the left of a bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter at a safe distance of not less than 3 feet between any portion of the vehicle and the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter, this paragraph authorizes the driver, if it is safe, to pass: (1) To the left of the center of the highway. (2) In a no-passing zone.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "'overtaking or passing' a road user proceeding the same way is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; it denotes the relative motion only. Here the pass is read while under way - the bodies side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero; a projection, not a contact or a distance) after the rider was ahead within the window - and once completed, from the observation at which the concept rises, within the window."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle, 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each admitted aggregate claimed whole."}, {"span": "b3", "atoms": ["rel.same_direction", "kin.speed"], "derived": [], "justification": "'proceeding' is the overtaken road user moving (kin.speed above the halt tolerance); 'in the same direction' is rel.same_direction ('headings aligned') between the subject and it."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a motor vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'). 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": [], "justification": "'only one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction' is the count of lanes in the direction of a lane (st.lane) the overtaken rider occupies (rel.occupies) being the stated one (st.lane_adjacency, 'the count of lanes in that direction'). 'traffic' names the users of the lane; no membership is read."}, {"span": "b9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "rel.bearing"], "derived": ["drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier"], "justification": "'move again to the right side of the highway': having moved out to the left of the rider (rel.bearing from the subject, lateral component negative: the rider on its right), the subject turns back toward the side the rider keeps: drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier(subject, L) for a lane L (st.lane) the rider occupies (rel.occupies) - 'a, moving, points to the right of the designated direction of travel of carrier region r by more than a tolerance'. The concept says nothing of whether the subject occupies L, so it reads a move back toward the rider's lane from the opposing lane or from the left part of the rider's lane alike. 'again' fixes the order: the subject first had the rider on its right."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b10", "standard": "until the vehicle is safely clear of the overtaken bicycle", "concepts": ["rel.surface_gap", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "kin.speed", "env.ice_or_snow", "env.wet_road", "env.precipitation"], "params": ["p.following_headway_dry", "p.following_headway_wet", "p.following_headway_ice"], "convention": "time headway: the subject (the vehicle) is safely clear of the overtaken rider where the rider is behind it (rel.bearing longitudinal component negative, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative) with a gap between the bodies (rel.surface_gap) of at least the rider's speed times the following headway for the surface - ice or snow, else wet road or precipitation, else dry - so that the rider, following, keeps the headway a following road user keeps", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_1", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2a", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11",